# Compound Learnings

## Read at Session Start

Before starting work, read the last 20 entries of `.sdlc/learnings/LEARNINGS.jsonl`.
These contain hard-won lessons from previous sessions. Do not repeat past mistakes.

## Write After Significant Work

After completing a feature, fixing a non-trivial bug, or discovering a pattern:

1. Propose 1-3 learnings to the developer
2. On approval, append to `.sdlc/learnings/LEARNINGS.jsonl`:

```json
{"timestamp":"<ISO-8601>","type":"pattern|mistake|convention|gotcha","desc":"<concise lesson>","context":"<file or area>"}
```

## Types

- **pattern**: A reusable approach that worked well
- **mistake**: Something that failed — prevent repetition
- **convention**: A project-specific standard discovered or established
- **gotcha**: A non-obvious behavior or edge case

## Rules

- Keep entries concise (one line each, <200 chars for desc)
- Never duplicate an existing entry
- Remove obsolete entries during updates (with developer approval)
- Entries are project knowledge — never include secrets, credentials, or PII

